{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1411433-can-someone-summarize-keys-to-the-supernal-tarot-for-me","id":1411433,"title":"Can someone summarize Keys to the Supernal Tarot for me?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-09-01T14:36:47-07:00","id":1411433,"title":"Can someone summarize Keys to the Supernal Tarot for me?","content":"Like specifically is there any setting info connected to the various cards and their images? I\u2019m thinking about buying it.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7967_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7967\" data-vbnamecard=\"7967\">Scarlet Witch</a> Mentioning you cause you know a lot about MtAw","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T14:45:55-07:00","id":1411434,"title":"","content":"Just checked it out on DTRPG. This sounds awesome! I would still defo love some more details though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T15:31:08-07:00","id":1411442,"title":"","content":"It covers the symbolism of the Paths, why they have such cards, what they mean and how to build the feel of their Mysteries. It also covers Legacies themed on counseling.The first is Mimir's Voice, focused on advice and pacifism. It has a very interesting idea, but the justification for Forces and the Attainments are all over the place.<br /> <br /> The other is the Illuminated Path, which sees Awakening as a spectrum, so they seek to guide and protect Sleepers as they walk down this road. While Spirit makes a lot of sense to allow Sleepers to interact with and be guarded against spiritual manipulation, I think Prime, with its purview of revelation and ability to grant magical senses, would be more suited to the theme than Forces.<br /> <br /> The last one is the Roses of Eden, which is an iconoclastic Legacy that breaks with Diamond doctrine, but its anti-establishment focus normally alienate them even from the Free Council. Their Attainments have a communal feel to them and are pretty interesting.<br /> <br /> The book also includes two more that stand on their own. The Whipping Boys try to reach ecstatic clarity through pain. Their Attainments focus on boosting physical actions, but are less practical than the Perfected Adepts. Like the Carnival Melancholy and Fallen Pillar, it feels like they don't get enough for their troubles.<br /> <br /> The other is the Celestial Masters, astronomers and navigators whose Attainments have a very Dr Manhattan feel to them.<br /> <br /> Hope that helps, its certainly worth a read.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-foru